cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Absolutus_V3 (modbench)"
abstract: >
  An open, reproducible benchmark and toolkit for cardinality-constrained
  module selection (QUBO / densest-k-subgraph style) on biologically
  structured networks. Compares classical solvers (random, greedy, simulated
  annealing, tabu, exact MILP) against QAOA with statevector and MPS
  (tensor-network) simulation at equal compute, with planted ground truth
  and a decoy-hub null model to expose degree/study-bias artefacts. v0.1.0
  ships 300 frozen instances (3 families x 5 sizes x 20 test seeds, sha256
  manifest), 114 aggregated cells with 20 seeds per cell and 95% bootstrap
  CIs, and a claims register where every claim cites a saved run.
authors:
  - family-names: "Absolutus V3 contributors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-28
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Katchaw451/Absolutus_V3"
url: "https://github.com/Katchaw451/Absolutus_V3"
keywords:
  - qubo
  - qaoa
  - tensor-networks
  - mps
  - benchmark
  - module-selection
  - bioinformatics
  - quantum-optimization
